00 BC\", \"Followed by: Yangshao culture\"); the page does not describe the transition.","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cishan_culture"},{"slug":"faiyum-merimde-neolithic","year":-5000,"type":"gain","text":"5000 BCE: the Merimde villagers settle the western Delta.","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Faiyum_A_culture"},{"slug":"jomon-period","year":-5000,"type":"rename","text":"5000 BCE: the Early Jōmon begins: \"Early (5,000-3,520 BC)\"; \"The Early Jōmon period saw an explosion in population\".","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jōmon_period"},{"slug":"linear-pottery-culture","year":-5000,"type":"rename","text":"5000 BCE: the Stroked pottery (Stichbandkeramik) phase, \"5000-4500 BC\", in which \"lines of punctures are substituted for the incised lines\"; \"a population collapse of 'enormous magnitude' after 5000 BC\".","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Linear_Pottery_culture"},{"slug":"linear-pottery-culture","year":-5000,"type":"loss","text":"5000 BCE: the Lengyel culture takes the middle Danube.","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Linear_Pottery_culture"},{"slug":"peiligang-culture","year":-5000,"type":"dissolve","text":"5000 BCE: the Peiligang gives way to the Yangshao culture (infobox \"7000-5000 BC\", \"Followed by: Yangshao culture\"); the page gives no transition.","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peiligang_culture"},{"slug":"yangshao-culture","year":-5000,"type":"gain","text":"5000 BCE: the Yangshao takes the Peiligang country; infobox \"Preceded by: Peiligang, Cishan, Dadiwan, and Baijia cultures\"; Yangshao harvesting knives were \"replacing earlier stone sickles found in the Peiligang and Cishan cultures\".","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yangshao_culture"},{"slug":"yangshao-culture","year":-5000,"type":"gain","text":"5000 BCE: the Yangshao takes the Cishan country of southern Hebei and northern Henan (Cishan infobox \"Followed by: Yangshao culture\").","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yangshao_culture"},{"slug":"yangshao-culture","year":-5000,"type":"gain","text":"5000 BCE: the rest of Henan, where \"The culture flourished mainly in Henan\" (Shuanghuaishu, the type region); no earlier state is named for it.","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yangshao_culture"},{"slug":"yangshao-culture","year":-5000,"type":"gain","text":"5000 BCE: the western Wei valley in Gansu, where the Dadiwan culture (5800-5400 BCE on the Dadiwan page) preceded the Yangshao; the Yangshao page names no date for the Dadiwan and the Dadiwan page says only that \"The Yangshao follows Dadiwan in the local sequence\", so the year is a bridge and the land passes through nobody's hands.","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yangshao_culture"}],"capitals":[]},"-4950":{"changes":[],"contests":[],"captions":[{"slug":"kuk-swamp-agriculture","year":-4950,"type":"rename","text":"4950 BCE: bananas and sugar cane join the crops at Kuk.","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kuk_Swamp"}],"capitals":[]},"-4940":{"changes":[{"cells":[113940,"113946-113952","113976-113977","114044-114045",114047,114049,"114233-114234","114237-114239",114247,"114251-114252",114261,"114263-114265",114267,114270,"114275-114276","114278-114281",114331,114333,"114335-114337","114346-114351","114359-114363",114365,"114373-114379","114429-114432",114435,114438,114440,"114442-114456",114471,"114473-114474",114477,"114527-114536","114538-114556","114559-114571","114573-114574","114918-114919","114922-114924","114946-114947",114949,114951,114953,"114955-114959","114995-114996",115000,115006,115008,115122,115124,115126,"115163-115166",115168,"115170-115171","115173-115183",115188,115190,115192,115196,"115198-115203","115207-115208",115211],"from":"linear-pottery-culture","to":null,"status":"neutral","event":"linear-pottery-culture/ledger/7","n":182},{"cells":[114345,114356,115013,115167,115169,"115193-115194","115204-115206",115210],"from":"linear-pottery-culture","to":null,"status":"neutral","event":"data/patches/m5000-m4901